# Linear governance — iPix

This file contains **stable governance rules**.

It must not be treated as the source of truth for changing workspace facts such as issue statuses, milestone dates, cycle windows, project health, ownership, or dependency state. Always read **live Linear** before making or recommending changes.

Companion: `.claude/skills/linear/` (hub) · `task-naming.mdc` (ID · SPEC — title) · live snapshot `tasks/linear/live-workspace-state.md` (summary only, may be stale).

## Live workspace state

Do not trust milestone dates, cycle windows, issue statuses, project health, or dependency examples written in this rule or in repo summaries.

Before mutation, read live Linear.

Repository live-state documents are summaries only and may be stale.

## Source-of-truth precedence

Use the authoritative source for each field:

| Information | Authority |
|-------------|-----------|
| Status, project, milestone, cycle, priority, owner | Live Linear |
| Code implementation | Current `origin/main` |
| Active implementation | Open PR and worktree evidence |
| Production behavior | Browser and production verification |
| Requirements and acceptance criteria | Canonical issue/spec |
| Progress documents | Reporting aid only |

When sources disagree, **report the conflict**. Do not silently overwrite either source.

## Access and capability discovery

| Prefer | Fallback |
|--------|----------|
| Linear MCP (`plugin-linear-linear`) | GraphQL with `LINEAR_API_KEY` when MCP cannot set a required field |

**Never** print `LINEAR_API_KEY` or tokens. **Never** delete projects/issues unless explicitly asked. Destructive/bulk changes → propose first, apply only after approval.

Before execution, **discover** the available Linear MCP methods for the current session. Do not assume every environment exposes the same create, update, milestone, cycle, project-relation, or patch operations.

Use GraphQL only when:

1. MCP cannot perform the required field update,
2. the mutation has been inspected,
3. affected entities are listed,
4. and approval exists for bulk or destructive changes.

Never use GraphQL as a shortcut around MCP safety checks.

## Naming and traceability

- Titles / first mention: **`IPI-NNN · SPEC — Plain English`** (`task-naming.mdc`).
- Team: **iPix1** (`IPI`).
- Local specs: `docs/linear/issues/IPI-*.md` when present.
- One **independently testable outcome** per issue and PR. Frontend, backend, tests, and documentation may remain together when they are required to deliver the same acceptance outcome. Split when work has different owners, release timing, rollback paths, or independent acceptance evidence.
- Still obey AGENTS.md: do not mix **unrelated** docs + production code, or two unrelated tasks, in one PR/commit.

## Project and initiative ownership

Attach issues to the project that **owns delivery**, not a historical epic. Resolve current project/initiative names via live Linear (`list_projects`, `list_initiatives`) — do not invent names.

Typical delivery surfaces (names may change — verify live):

| Project role | Examples of ownership |
|--------------|----------------------|
| Operator React / design parity | DESIGN V2 — Operator React Parity |
| Launch / onboarding / beta | MVP |
| Cloudflare / DNS / Workers | HOSTING |
| Provider routing | AI Platform — LLM Providers |

Initiatives: attach projects under the current operator initiative when appropriate; resolve via MCP before writing IDs.

## Milestones

Pattern: `{PROJECT_PREFIX}-M{n} · {Outcome}` with **targetDate** + ascending **sortOrder**.

Every **active DESIGN V2 delivery issue** should have exactly one outcome milestone.

Exceptions:

- Parent tracking issues that do not represent deliverable work
- Cross-project issues owned elsewhere
- Explicitly unscheduled backlog
- Duplicate, canceled, or completed historical issues

Do not assign a milestone only to improve project percentages.

Remap / re-date only with approval; then reassign the intended open set in one pass and verify counts against live Linear.

Clear `projectMilestone` on **Duplicate** / noise terminal issues when milestones distort progress %. Prefer clearing cycle membership on Dupes when stale.

Do not put backend-only tickets in a desktop-parity milestone or mobile tickets in a shell milestone without a stated reason.

Current dates and names: live Linear (or `tasks/linear/live-workspace-state.md` as a non-authoritative cache).

## Cycles

A cycle contains work expected to **start or materially progress** during that window.

Do not assign an issue solely because it is important. It must be:

- unblocked or expected to unblock during the cycle,
- small enough to progress meaningfully,
- owned,
- and supported by available capacity.

Todo and cycle membership are separate:

| Board state | Meaning |
|-------------|---------|
| Backlog | Unscheduled |
| Todo | Ready to start |
| In Progress | Actively executing |

Rules:

- Assign approved active items only; keep intentional exclusions outside the cycle.
- Preserved **Done** history in a cycle is OK; do not yank without ask.
- Clear stale cycles from Duplicate/Canceled issues.
- Do **not** create overlapping cycles (Linear rejects date overlap).
- HOLD / DNS cutover work stays out of beta cycles.

Current cycle name/window: live Linear (or live-state cache).

## Dependencies

Use Linear relations, not prose-only “depends on”:

| Relation | Meaning |
|----------|---------|
| `blocks` / `blockedBy` | Hard execution order |
| `relatedTo` | Soft link / context |
| `duplicateOf` | Canonical survivor; mark loser **Duplicate** |

Prefer `A blocks B` when B cannot ship before A (product prerequisite). After adding edges, scan for **cycles** among open issues; fix before leaving.

Completed blockers do not prevent execution and may preserve valuable history. Remove a dependency only when it is incorrect, duplicated, circular, or references work that was never a true prerequisite. **Do not** remove it merely because the blocking issue is Done.

Illustrative dependency patterns — **verify live before using**:

- Analytics overview may block campaign drill-down.
- Matching may block Talent Profile.
- Talent Profile may block Availability Editor.
- Planner read views may block safe mutation and responsive QA.

Never create an edge solely because it appears as an example in this rule.

## Status and completion evidence

| State | When |
|-------|------|
| Backlog | Unscheduled |
| Todo | Ready to start |
| In Progress | Active implementation |
| Done | ACs met + evidence (`origin/main`, tests, browser) — never status-copy alone |
| Duplicate | Loser of dedupe (`duplicateOf` set) |
| Canceled | Explicitly abandoned |

If evidence shows a Done issue has unmet acceptance criteria:

1. Record the exact missing acceptance criterion.
2. Verify the gap belongs to the same issue rather than a follow-up.
3. Propose reopening the issue.
4. Reopen only when explicitly approved, unless the current task specifically authorizes status correction.

## Progress documents

For Linear progress documents (e.g. DESIGN V2 HTML→React tracker):

1. Read the current document.
2. Identify exact outdated sections.
3. Patch only those sections when supported.
4. Use full replacement only when the complete current document has been preserved.
5. Re-read the document after saving.
6. Confirm links, milestone names, counts, and dates.

Repo trackers (`Universal-design-prompt-4/progress.md`, `todo.md`) are separate docs PRs — do not mix into a Linear-only pass unless asked.

## Project updates

After material governance changes (milestone remap, cycle rename, ownership moves), post a **project status update** with health (`onTrack` / `atRisk` / `offTrack`) and a plain-English table of what changed — when the MCP tool is available.

## HOLD representation

Linear has no native HOLD status in this workflow. “HOLD” means **all** of the following (verify live):

- Status: **Backlog**
- Project: **HOSTING** (or the live hosting project)
- Milestone: DNS cutover milestone
- No active cycle
- Not assigned as current execution
- Description or latest status update explicitly says HOLD
- Required blockers remain unresolved

Canonical example (verify title/fields live): **IPI-631 · CF-MIG-810 — Move ipix.co to Cloudflare**. Do not start or cycle-assign HOLD DNS work during beta cleanup.

## Read-only verification workflow

```text
1. Discover MCP capabilities for this session
2. get_project (+ milestones) / list_cycles / list_issues (filtered)
3. Spot-check ownership, cycle membership, milestones on the open set
4. Dependency + circular-block detection among open issues
5. Compare Linear vs origin/main + repo trackers (label STALE; do not silently “fix” docs)
6. Return PASS / NEEDS FIXES — propose fixes; mutate only when asked
```

## Approved mutation workflow

```text
1. Confirm approval / task authorizes the mutation
2. Milestones rename/create/re-date → reassign intended open issues → verify counts live
3. Cycle membership (active + exclusions)
4. Dependency edges (no cycles; preserve valid Done history)
5. Duplicate milestone/cycle cleanup when distorting boards
6. Patch progress tracker sections + optional project update
7. Issue description notes when status/evidence drifted
8. Return LINEAR FIX VERDICT with what changed / skipped
```

## Issue creation checklist

- [ ] Dedupe search by title/identifier first
- [ ] Full title format + team IPI
- [ ] Correct project + milestone (when active delivery) + optional cycle
- [ ] `blockedBy` / `blocks` for hard order (verified live)
- [ ] Initiative only when the project attachment warrants it
- [ ] Labels that match track — don’t invent

